    --dnd-bg-color: var(--color-selected-light);
    --dnd-border-color: var(--color-selected-dark);

    background-color: var(--dnd-bg-color);
    outline: 2px dashed var(--dnd-border-color);
    outline-offset: -2px;
    transition: background-color 200ms;
    z-index: 1;
  }
}
```

The Stimulus controller likely named `drag-and-drop`, file `drag_and_drop_controller.js` (Stimulus naming: `data-controller="drag-and-drop"` resolves to `drag_and_drop_controller.js`? Stimulus identifier conversion: dashes to underscores -> drag_and_drop_controller). Yes.

It likely:
- static targets = [ "draggable", "dropContainer"? ]
- static classes = [ "draggedItem", "hoverContainer" ]
- static values maybe.
- connects by setting `draggable` on cards? Or views set draggable attributes.

Design hooks in view likely: `data-controller="drag-and-drop"` on `.card-columns`; `data-drag-and-drop-target="draggable"` on cards? Hmm, but cards are inside columns rendered from frames; the controller element is the ancestor, so it can query descendants with `[draggable]` or a data attr.

Maybe the controller uses HTML5 drag events: `dragstart`, `dragend`, `dragover`, `dragleave`, `drop`. With delegation on element:
```
dragstart->drag-and-drop#dragStart
dragend->drag-and-drop#dragEnd
dragover->drag-and-drop#dragOver
dragleave->drag-and-drop#dragLeave
drop->drag-and-drop#drop
```
On dragstart, find closest `.card`, add class `drag-and-drop__dragged-item`, set `dataTransfer.setData`, maybe set drag image.
On dragover target column `.cards`, preventDefault, add `drag-and-drop__hover-container` to column.
On drop, determine target column data; move card element to target `.cards__list`; immediately POST/PATCH to server; remove classes. Use fetch with `responseKind: "turbo-stream"`? If response is turbo-stream with a page refresh? Actually endpoints might respond with turbo streams (e.g., triage create currently renders `format.html` redirect for HTML; `format.json` head no_content; no turbo_stream format for triage create!). Hmm, `Cards::TriagesController#create` responds only html and json. `not_nows#create` responds turbo_stream and json. `closures#create` responds turbo_stream and json.

For DnD, likely a JSON request (fetch) is fine. "no waiting on the save" -> send request in background, ignore response. But then if save fails, board is wrong; acceptable for issue.

But the requirement "nothing shifting afterwards" also implies disabling broadcast-triggered re-render? The card update triggers `broadcasts_refreshes` -> page morph. If server sort order doesn't match optimistic placement, shift. So JS must insert at the right place matching server sort order. What is server order in columns? `@column.cards.active.latest.with_golden_first.preloaded` -> active cards (open, published, not postponed) with golden first, then latest (last_active_at desc). Dropping into column triggers triage event -> last_active_at now -> card first among non-golden. So insert at top (after any golden cards). Hmm, but if target column has golden cards first, card should be inserted after golden cards. `with_golden_first` scope likely orders golden first. Let's check.

